# Barre Progression: I-vi-IV-V (repertoire plan: st-barre-progression). An original 16-bar study
# on the I-vi-IV-V progression. Bars 1-8 in A: A (x02220), the F#m barre at fret 2 (244222),
# D (xx0232) and E (022100). Bars 9-16 the same progression in C, every chord a barre: C as an
# A-shape barre at fret 3 (x35553), Am as an E-shape minor barre at fret 5 (577555), F as the
# E-shape barre at fret 1 (133211) and G as the E-shape barre at fret 3 (355433).
# The folk strum in every one-chord bar: down, down-up, (miss), up, down-up. Bars 7 and 15 change
# to V on beat 3 (down, down-up for each chord), and each half ends on its I chord.
# The teacher's bass plays the root on beat 1 and the fifth on beat 3.
title: Barre Progression: I-vi-IV-V
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original study on the I-vi-IV-V progression, in A and in C
licence: Original study for Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 6
tags: barre chords, i-vi-iv-v, folk strum, transposing
